   "text": {
    "L1": "Houses are not built the same everywhere. They are built to suit the weather and land of a place.",
    "L2": "A roof is not only for looks. Where rain or snow is heavy, a sloping roof lets it slide off.",
    "L3": "Where it hardly rains, a flat roof can work. People may use it for drying things or sleeping.",
    "L4": "In flood-prone parts of Assam, houses stand on stilts. This keeps them above flood water and damp ground.",
    "L5": "People often use materials found nearby, such as bamboo, mud, stone and wood. That is why houses in different places look different.",
    "L6": "Thick mud or stone walls help keep a house cool on hot days and warmer on cold nights.",
    "L7": "So one house cannot suit every place. First look at the weather, land and nearby materials.",
    "L8": "Now check your idea. Which roof suits a place with heavy rain?"
   },
